<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Campaign</p><h1 class="enc-title">Operation Torch</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1942</span> · Also known as Allied invasion of French North Africa · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Operation Torch was the Allied invasion of French <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a> in November 1942, with landings around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/casablanca">Casablanca</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oran">Oran</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a>. American and British forces met brief resistance from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vichy">Vichy</a> French troops before Admiral Darlan agreed to a ceasefire. It opened a new front in North <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>, led to the German occupation of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and was followed by the Tunisian campaign.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/operation-torch.jpg" alt="Operation Torch" width="320" height="124" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Operation_Torch_-_map.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
